Blend markers multiplicatively on projector and zoom panel

Purpose: upstream #1730 multiplies highlighter (marker) strokes with
the paper and ink below on the main canvas. The projector and the zoom
panel draw through their own raster cache and kept plain alpha, so
markers looked different there.

Approach: draw_strokes_cached mirrors the main canvas. It takes the
view's paper as a closure and nests one GSK multiply blend per marker:
paper and regular ink form the bottom, each marker the top of its
blend. Cached rasters and immediate runs work per key as before.

Constraints: builds on projector-tablet (raster cache) and
manim-slides (live strokes). No file format change. The test needs a
display for GTK and passes trivially without one.

